{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1842","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Tenzing and Random Operations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yet another random problem."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tenzing has an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$ and an integer $$$v$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tenzing will perform the following operation $$$m$$$ times:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose an integer $$$i$$$ such that $$$1 \\leq i \\leq n$$$ uniformly at random. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For all $$$j$$$ such that $$$i \\leq j \\leq n$$$, set $$$a_j := a_j + v$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tenzing wants to know the expected value of $$$\\prod_{i=1}^n a_i$$$ after performing the $$$m$$$ operations, modulo $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, let $$$M = 10^9+7$$$. It can be shown that the answer can be expressed as an irreducible fraction $$$\\frac{p}{q}$$$, where $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ are integers and $$$q \\not \\equiv 0 \\pmod{M}$$$. Output the integer equal to $$$p \\cdot q^{-1} \\bmod M$$$. In other words, output the integer $$$x$$$ that $$$0 \\le x \\lt M$$$ and $$$x \\cdot q \\equiv p \\pmod{M}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ and $$$v$$$ ($$$1\\leq n\\leq 5000$$$, $$$1\\leq m,v\\leq 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of input contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$1\\leq a_i\\leq 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output the expected value of $$$\\prod_{i=1}^n a_i$$$ modulo $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2 5\n2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n84\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 7 9\n9 9 8 2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n975544726\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are three types of $$$a$$$ after performing all the $$$m$$$ operations : "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1. $$$a_1=2,a_2=12$$$ with $$$\\frac{1}{4}$$$ probability."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2. $$$a_1=a_2=12$$$ with $$$\\frac{1}{4}$$$ probability."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3. $$$a_1=7,a_2=12$$$ with $$$\\frac{1}{2}$$$ probability."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So the expected value of $$$a_1\\cdot a_2$$$ is $$$\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (24+144) + \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 84=84$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"1842G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1842/problem/G"}